  "ears": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - `positions` states where the ears bolt, for the Rack Builder. The backbone is the mounting plane and the duct stands 113.3 mm in front of it (the end view of the steel datasheet, page 4; see `full-depth`). `at` is 113.3, so all of the depth is in front of the rail. This states a placement; no dimension changed."
  },
  "fingers": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - ten fingers a row. The plan draws their stems 69.6 px apart, 44.4 mm, and five two-finger mouldings 443.5 over all; ten at 44.4 would run past the 440 cover, so the pitch is taken as 44.0 and the row fills the body between the ears, 0.4 mm a pitch short of the drawing. A finger is a stem 10.2 wide and a T head 39.4 wide, leaving a 4.6 neck between heads. On the plan the stem forks into two legs that meet the moulded block 28 mm from the back; the fork is drawn as the stem running straight to the block. The square windows in the blocks are not drawn."
  },
  "front": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawing - the cover, fitted, as the front view of the drawing draws it: 440 x 51 with four hinge clips, two on the top edge and two on the bottom, staggered. The fingers stand in two rows 9.0 thick, 4.7 in from the top and bottom of the cover, read off the end view, which draws the two finger walls 14 px thick with their outer faces 66 px apart. The `duct` guide is the 23.6 mm between the rows."
  },
  "full-depth": {
